# l6-p1-bid-scope-types-ts

## SOURCE OF TRUTH WARNING

- **Spec**: `docs/strategy/layers/layer-6-request-pipeline-automation.md` — §1.4 (BidScopePayload type + SideEffectClass union), §1.6 (BidWorkflow / BidDocument / SubmissionResult / DraftSaveResult / PortalStateVerification interfaces), §1.6.3 (CompanyProfile) (PRIMARY)
- **TDD**: `...l6-request-pipeline-automation-tdd.md` — §7.1 `L6-T-bid_workflow_states-030/031/032/033`, §7.3 `L6-T-portal_side_effects-001` (CROSS-PHASE COVERAGE; primary ownership in Phase 5 package test files)
- **Strategy**: Phase 1, "shared bid types" routing batch
- **Bootstrap**: §6 — manifest `new_modules_ts.bidding.bid-scope-types.ts` purpose note

## Coordination Protocol

`bin/br-claim` / `bin/br-complete`. Sync via `bin/br-sync`.

## Context

`packages/bidding/bid-scope-types.ts` is the TypeScript home for `BidScopePayload`, `SideEffectClass` union, `BidDocument`, `BidWorkflow` interface, `SubmissionResult`, `DraftSaveResult`, `PortalStateVerification`. These types are pure exports — no runtime logic. They are consumed by Phase 4 (skill `result.schema.json` references `SubmissionResult` shape), Phase 2 (Rust IPC handler accepts `BidScopePayload` at the public boundary), and Phase 5 (`workflow-registry.ts` / `procontract-workflow.ts` build on these types). PER MANIFEST CRITICAL DEPENDENCY: these types MUST land in Phase 1, NOT Phase 5.

## Spec Requirements (verbatim)

From spec §1.4 (BidScopePayload + SideEffectClass):

```typescript
interface BidScopePayload {
  processId: string
  lotIds: string[]
  candidateIds: string[]
  selectedQuoteIds: string[]
  companyProfileVersion: string
  bidPortalType: string                // currently only 'procontract'
  portalOpportunityRef: string
  reviewRequired: boolean              // defaults true per Decision 5
  decisionBasisHash: string            // 64-char SHA-256
  sideEffectCap: SideEffectClass       // defaults REMOTE_DRAFT per Decision 5
}

type SideEffectClass =
  | 'READ_ONLY'
  | 'REMOTE_DRAFT'
  | 'NOTIFICATION_OR_LOCK'
  | 'LEGAL_DECLARATION'
  | 'FORMAL_SUBMISSION'
  | 'FUNDS_COMMITTED'
```

From spec §1.6 (BidWorkflow / BidDocument / SubmissionResult / DraftSaveResult / PortalStateVerification — see source for the full type declarations, copied verbatim).


Spec FR traceability: L6-FR-1.4.1 through L6-FR-1.4.12 define every BidScopePayload and SideEffectClass field implemented by this TypeScript type bead.

## TDD Tests Owned

Primary ownership of the runtime FK/shape tests lives in Phase 5 package test files. This bead provides the types those tests import.

Indirect coverage:
- L6-T-bid_workflow_states-030: BidScopePayload validates all required references.
- L6-T-bid_workflow_states-031: decisionBasisHash is 64-character SHA-256.
- L6-T-bid_workflow_states-032: reviewRequired defaults true, sideEffectCap defaults REMOTE_DRAFT.
- L6-T-bid_workflow_states-033: bid_scope_json persisted but not exposed in projection.
- L6-T-portal_side_effects-001: SideEffectClass ordering exactly READ_ONLY < REMOTE_DRAFT < NOTIFICATION_OR_LOCK < LEGAL_DECLARATION < FORMAL_SUBMISSION < FUNDS_COMMITTED.

## Files to Create/Modify

- **Create:** `packages/bidding/bid-scope-types.ts` — all 7 types verbatim from spec §1.4 and §1.6.
- **Verify only:** `packages/contracts-schema/src/index.ts:463` — consider whether to re-export from contracts-schema. RECOMMENDATION per manifest: live in packages/bidding only and re-export from contracts-schema ONLY if a non-bidding package needs them (defer that decision until a concrete consumer exists).

## Implementation Details

`bid-scope-types.ts` (full, verbatim from spec §1.4 + §1.6):

```typescript
export interface BidScopePayload {
  processId: string;
  lotIds: string[];
  candidateIds: string[];
  selectedQuoteIds: string[];
  companyProfileVersion: string;
  bidPortalType: string;            // currently only 'procontract'
  portalOpportunityRef: string;
  reviewRequired: boolean;          // defaults true per Decision 5
  decisionBasisHash: string;        // 64-char SHA-256
  sideEffectCap: SideEffectClass;   // defaults REMOTE_DRAFT per Decision 5
}

export type SideEffectClass =
  | 'READ_ONLY'
  | 'REMOTE_DRAFT'
  | 'NOTIFICATION_OR_LOCK'
  | 'LEGAL_DECLARATION'
  | 'FORMAL_SUBMISSION'
  | 'FUNDS_COMMITTED';

export const SIDE_EFFECT_CLASS_ORDER: SideEffectClass[] = [
  'READ_ONLY',
  'REMOTE_DRAFT',
  'NOTIFICATION_OR_LOCK',
  'LEGAL_DECLARATION',
  'FORMAL_SUBMISSION',
  'FUNDS_COMMITTED',
];

export interface BidDocument {
  documentType: string;
  fileName: string;
  filePath: string;
  contentHash: string;
  expiryDate?: string;
  issuingBody?: string;
}

export interface SubmissionResult {
  submitted: boolean;
  confirmationRef?: string;
  finalSideEffectClass: SideEffectClass;
  screenshotPaths: string[];
  portalTimestamp?: string;
}

export interface DraftSaveResult {
  draftSaved: boolean;
  portalDraftRef?: string;
  sideEffectClass: SideEffectClass;
}

export interface PortalStateVerification {
  opportunityFound: boolean;
  existingDraftDetected: boolean;
  existingSubmissionDetected: boolean;
  portalStatus: string;
}

export interface BidWorkflow {
  portalType: string;
  // Method signatures only — Phase 5 procontract-workflow.ts implements
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `packages/bidding/bid-scope-types.ts` exists with all 7 types verbatim from spec.
- [ ] `BidScopePayload` has all 10 fields per spec §1.4.
- [ ] `SideEffectClass` is exactly the 6 string-literal union per spec.
- [ ] `SIDE_EFFECT_CLASS_ORDER` constant ordered exactly READ_ONLY < REMOTE_DRAFT < NOTIFICATION_OR_LOCK < LEGAL_DECLARATION < FORMAL_SUBMISSION < FUNDS_COMMITTED.
- [ ] `cd packages/bidding && bun run build` succeeds.
- [ ] `cd packages/bidding && bun run lint` passes.
- [ ] Rust `crates/daemon/src/bid_workflow/types.rs` (sibling bead `l6-p1-bid-workflow-module-skeleton`) shape matches these TS types (manual cross-check until type-bridging tests land in Phase 5).
- [ ] No re-export from `packages/contracts-schema` yet (defer until a non-bidding consumer needs them).

## Dependencies

- **Blocked by:** `l6-p1-bidding-package-scaffold`.
- **Blocks:** `l6-p2-ipc-trigger-handler` (Rust handler accepts BidScopePayload), `l6-p4-result-checkpoint-schemas` (result.schema.json references SubmissionResult), `l6-p5-workflow-registry-ts`, `l6-p5-procontract-workflow-ts`, `l6-p5-bid-workflow-states-test-ts`, `l6-p5-portal-side-effects-test-ts`, `l6-p5-bid-readiness-gate-test-ts`, `l6-p1-foundation-review-gate`.
- **Phase:** 1.

# l6-p2-ipc-trigger-handler

## SOURCE OF TRUTH WARNING

- **Spec**: `docs/strategy/layers/layer-6-request-pipeline-automation.md` — §1.5.1 (Start Bid in desktop), §1.5.2 (DaemonBridge trigger), §1.10.3 (explicit scope), §1.10.6 (L5 readiness gate at IPC boundary) (PRIMARY)
- **TDD**: `...-tdd.md` — §7.7 `L6-T-ipc_trigger_bid_workflow-001..003`, §8.2 IPC rejection shape (PRIMARY)
- **Strategy**: Phase 2, "`trigger_bid_workflow` IPC" routing batch
- **Bootstrap**: §6 — manifest `daemon_ipc_handlers_jobs` notes (existing `trigger_ingestion` at jobs.rs:45 + `trigger_enrichment` at jobs.rs:95 as reference patterns)

## Coordination Protocol

`bin/br-claim` / `bin/br-complete`. Sync via `bin/br-sync`.

## Context

`crates/daemon/src/ipc/handlers/jobs.rs` is the IPC entry point for job triggers. Existing handlers `trigger_ingestion` (line 45) and `trigger_enrichment` (line 95) follow the pattern: validate request params → run readiness pre-check → if blocked, return structured rejection envelope with `code`, `message`, `retryable=false`, `blockers[]`; if eligible, build EnqueueJobRequest via the runner builder, enqueue once, return `continuation_job_id`. This bead adds `trigger_bid_workflow(TriggerBidWorkflowParams { process_id, bid_scope, ... })` following the same pattern. The readiness pre-check body itself is Phase 3 (`l6-p3-readiness-evaluator`); this bead just wires the pre-check call site and ensures the rejection envelope matches the existing handler-style shape.

## Spec Requirements (verbatim)

**L6-FR-1.5.1 — Operator clicks "Start Bid" in desktop control panel.**
- AC: Desktop action is available only when readiness pre-check returns eligible or a structured override path is explicitly available.

**L6-FR-1.5.2 — Desktop sends trigger command to daemon via DaemonBridge.**
- AC: Command carries `process_id` and explicit bid scope; mutation is not executed by the web portal.

**L6-FR-1.10.3 — Bid workflow carries explicit scope.**
- AC: IPC trigger schema and readiness gate require non-empty `processId`, `lotIds`, `candidateIds`, `selectedQuoteIds`, `portalOpportunityRef`, `decisionBasisHash`, and `sideEffectCap`; FK ownership is checked before writing `bid_scope_json`.

## TDD Tests Owned

- **L6-T-ipc_trigger_bid_workflow-001** (T2/T3): New IPC route and TypeScript bridge method validate the `trigger_bid_workflow` request and response schema.
- **L6-T-ipc_trigger_bid_workflow-002** (T2/T3): IPC handler runs readiness pre-check before any `EnqueueJobRequest`; a failed gate returns the existing handler error envelope with `code`, `message`, `retryable=false`, and structured blocker codes, and no `workflow_jobs` row is created.
- **L6-T-ipc_trigger_bid_workflow-003** (T2/T3): Eligible request enqueues exactly one workflow job via `EnqueueJobRequest` with `kind="run_bid_workflow"`, bid scope, cap, continuation metadata, and returns `continuation_job_id`.

## Files to Create/Modify

- **Modify:** `crates/daemon/src/ipc/handlers/jobs.rs` — add `trigger_bid_workflow` handler.
- **Modify:** `crates/daemon/src/ipc/command_router.rs` — register the new `trigger_bid_workflow` route.
- **Modify:** `apps/desktop/src/lib/transport.ts` — add the matching TypeScript request/response types for the new `trigger_bid_workflow` route. (TS-side bridge lives in transport.ts at that path, not a separate file.)

## Implementation Details

```rust
// In crates/daemon/src/ipc/handlers/jobs.rs
// Mirror trigger_ingestion (jobs.rs:45) + trigger_enrichment (jobs.rs:95) shape:
// SYNC `pub fn` (not async); takes (&mut JobsHandlerContext, &Params, &str idempotency_key);
// returns Result<MutationAck, JobsHandlerError>.
pub fn trigger_bid_workflow(
    context: &mut JobsHandlerContext<'_>,
    params: &TriggerBidWorkflowParams,
    idempotency_key: &str,
) -> std::result::Result<MutationAck, JobsHandlerError> {
    // 1. Validate request shape — invariant L6-FR-1.10.3
    if params.bid_scope.lot_ids.is_empty()
        || params.bid_scope.candidate_ids.is_empty()
        || params.bid_scope.selected_quote_ids.is_empty()
        || params.bid_scope.portal_opportunity_ref.is_empty()
        || params.bid_scope.decision_basis_hash.len() != 64 {
        return Err(JobsHandlerError::invalid_request(...));
    }

    // 2. Run readiness pre-check (Phase 3 body)
    let readiness = bid_workflow::evaluate_bid_readiness(
        runtime,
        &params.bid_scope,
    ).await?;
    if !readiness.eligible {
        return Ok(TriggerBidWorkflowResponse::Blocked {
            code: "conflict",
            message: "bid workflow readiness failed",
            retryable: false,
            blockers: readiness.blockers,
        });
    }

    // 3. Build EnqueueJobRequest (sibling bead)
    let enqueue_req = enqueue_bid_workflow_request(
        &params.bid_scope,
        &params.operator_id,
        &readiness.resolved_company_profile,
        &params.bid_documents,
        &params.stage_run_id,
    )?;

    // 4. Enqueue (idempotency_key prevents duplicate enqueue)
    let job_id = runtime.job_runner.enqueue_job(enqueue_req).await?;

    Ok(TriggerBidWorkflowResponse::Enqueued {
        continuation_job_id: job_id,
    })
}
```

Blocked response shape (matches existing handler-style envelope per TDD §8.2):

```json
{
  "code": "conflict",
  "message": "bid workflow readiness failed",
  "retryable": false,
  "blockers": [
    {"code": "CLASSIFICATION_AMBIGUOUS", "source": "landed_cost_estimates", "overrideable": false}
  ]
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `trigger_bid_workflow` handler registered with the IPC router.
- [ ] TypeScript bridge has matching request/response types.
- [ ] Request validation rejects missing/empty `lotIds`, `candidateIds`, `selectedQuoteIds`, `portalOpportunityRef`, `decisionBasisHash` (not 64 chars), and missing `sideEffectCap`.
- [ ] Readiness pre-check runs BEFORE `EnqueueJobRequest` build (verify by JobRunner::enqueue_job() spy: not called on blocked path).
- [ ] Blocked response includes structured `blockers[]` with stable machine-readable codes.
- [ ] Eligible response includes `continuation_job_id`.
- [ ] No `workflow_jobs` row created on blocked path (assert via test DB query).
- [ ] `cargo test --test ipc_trigger_bid_workflow` passes.
- [ ] `L6-T-ipc_trigger_bid_workflow-001/002/003` pass.

## Dependencies

- **Blocked by:** `l6-p2-enqueue-builder` (uses the builder).
- **Blocks:** `l6-p2-readiness-precheck-wiring`, `l6-p2-daemon-runtime-review-gate`, `l6-p6-desktop-start-bid-control` (desktop UI calls this handler).
- **Phase:** 2.

# l6-p2-readiness-precheck-wiring

## SOURCE OF TRUTH WARNING

- **Spec**: `docs/strategy/layers/layer-6-request-pipeline-automation.md` — §1.3 prerequisite check (constitutional 5+2 gates), §1.10.1/.6 invariants (PRIMARY)
- **TDD**: `...-tdd.md` — §7.7 `L6-T-ipc_trigger_bid_workflow-002` (precheck before enqueue + envelope shape) (PRIMARY)
- **Strategy**: Phase 2, "handler rejection shape" routing batch
- **Bootstrap**: §6 — manifest `daemon_main` notes (L5 readiness raw checks at main.rs:5256-5260, 5510-5527, 5537-5542, 5781-5787)

## Coordination Protocol

`bin/br-claim` / `bin/br-complete`. Sync via `bin/br-sync`.

## Context

Phase 2 wires the readiness pre-check call site at the IPC handler boundary. The actual readiness evaluator BODY is Phase 3 (`l6-p3-readiness-evaluator` — composes existing L5 raw checks plus L6 bid-specific gates). This bead's responsibility is to ensure the readiness call site exists in the IPC handler AND the CLI trigger AND that the rejection envelope is the existing handler-style shape (not a new shape) AND that the readiness call happens BEFORE any `EnqueueJobRequest` build. The Phase 1 stub `bid_workflow::evaluate_bid_readiness` is called; its body is `unimplemented!("Phase 3")` until Phase 3 lands. This bead also tests the call-site contract by stubbing the evaluator to return both eligible and blocked verdicts in tests.

## Spec Requirements (verbatim)

**Prerequisite check (constitutional)**: Bid workflow CANNOT start unless all five L5→L6 readiness blockers are clear plus two quality gates. Per spec §1.3.


Spec FR traceability: L6-FR-1.3.16 and L6-FR-1.10.6 require readiness pre-checks before bid workflow enqueue and forbid bypassing L5 blocker gates.

## TDD Tests Owned

- **L6-T-ipc_trigger_bid_workflow-002** (T2/T3, partial — call-site contract): IPC handler runs readiness pre-check before any `EnqueueJobRequest`; a failed gate returns the existing handler error envelope with `code`, `message`, `retryable=false`, and structured blocker codes, and no `workflow_jobs` row is created.

(Full evaluator body is owned by Phase 3 `l6-p3-readiness-evaluator`.)

## Files to Create/Modify

- **Verify only:** `crates/daemon/src/ipc/handlers/jobs.rs` `trigger_bid_workflow` handler — confirm `bid_workflow::evaluate_bid_readiness(...)` is called BEFORE any `enqueue_bid_workflow_request(...)` call.
- **Create:** `crates/daemon/tests/ipc_trigger_bid_workflow.rs` — assert call ordering via a stubbed evaluator that returns Blocked and verify NO `workflow_jobs` row exists, then re-run with Eligible and verify exactly one row exists.

## Implementation Details

The call-site contract is:

```rust
// In IPC handler (must be in this order)
let readiness = bid_workflow::evaluate_bid_readiness(runtime, &params.bid_scope).await?;
if !readiness.eligible {
    return Ok(TriggerBidWorkflowResponse::Blocked { ... blockers: readiness.blockers });
}
// ONLY now build + enqueue
let enqueue_req = enqueue_bid_workflow_request(...)?;
let job_id = runtime.job_runner.enqueue_job(enqueue_req).await?;
```

The test asserts:

```rust
#[tokio::test]
async fn trigger_bid_workflow_runs_readiness_before_enqueue() {
    let db = TestStateDb::new().await.unwrap();
    let runtime = make_test_runtime_with_blocked_readiness(&db).await;
    let params = make_valid_trigger_params();

    let response = trigger_bid_workflow(params, &runtime).await.unwrap();
    assert!(matches!(response, TriggerBidWorkflowResponse::Blocked { .. }));

    // No workflow_jobs row created
    let count: i64 = db.conn().query_one("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workflow_jobs", []).await.unwrap();
    assert_eq!(count, 0);
}

#[tokio::test]
async fn trigger_bid_workflow_enqueues_on_eligible() {
    let db = TestStateDb::new().await.unwrap();
    let runtime = make_test_runtime_with_eligible_readiness(&db).await;
    let params = make_valid_trigger_params();

    let response = trigger_bid_workflow(params, &runtime).await.unwrap();
    assert!(matches!(response, TriggerBidWorkflowResponse::Enqueued { .. }));

    let count: i64 = db.conn().query_one("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workflow_jobs WHERE kind = 'run_bid_workflow'", []).await.unwrap();
    assert_eq!(count, 1);
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] In `trigger_bid_workflow`, `evaluate_bid_readiness` is called BEFORE `enqueue_bid_workflow_request` (verify by code reading + integration test).
- [ ] Blocked verdict returns rejection envelope without invoking `JobRunner::enqueue_job`.
- [ ] Eligible verdict invokes `JobRunner::enqueue_job` exactly once.
- [ ] No `workflow_jobs` row exists after a blocked trigger.
- [ ] Exactly one `workflow_jobs` row exists after an eligible trigger (idempotency key prevents duplicates).
- [ ] CLI trigger (`l6-p2-cli-manual-trigger`) routes through the same boundary.
- [ ] `cargo test --test ipc_trigger_bid_workflow` (or focused target) passes.

## Dependencies

- **Blocked by:** `l6-p2-ipc-trigger-handler`.
- **Blocks:** `l6-p2-daemon-runtime-review-gate`, `l6-p3-readiness-evaluator` (Phase 3 fills the stub body).
- **Phase:** 2.

# l6-p2-cli-manual-trigger

## SOURCE OF TRUTH WARNING

- **Spec**: (silent on CLI but manifest `new_modules_rust` lists `--run-bid-workflow <bid-job-id>` CLI subcommand for ops/manual recovery)
- **TDD**: `...-tdd.md` — §7.6 `L6-T-daemon_runner-010` (CLI/manual trigger path) (PRIMARY)
- **Strategy**: Phase 2, "CLI/manual trigger" routing batch
- **Bootstrap**: §6 — manifest `new_modules_rust` lists CLI subcommand

## Coordination Protocol

`bin/br-claim` / `bin/br-complete`. Sync via `bin/br-sync`.

## Context

For ops/manual recovery, the daemon binary exposes `--run-bid-workflow <bid-job-id>`. This CLI subcommand mirrors existing CLI subcommands in `main.rs` and routes through the SAME readiness boundary as the IPC handler (no readiness bypass). It is intended for re-running a previously-blocked bid job after manual reconciliation (e.g., operator clears stale-decision flag → CLI re-triggers without going through desktop).

## Spec Requirements (verbatim)

(Spec does not name the CLI flag; bootstrap manifest specifies it as L6 deliverable for ops.)


Spec FR traceability: L6-FR-1.10.6 — L5 readiness gate failures block `ready_to_bid`; the CLI path must route through this same readiness boundary before enqueue.

## TDD Tests Owned

- **L6-T-daemon_runner-010** (T2): CLI/manual trigger path supports `--run-bid-workflow` without bypassing readiness gates.

## Files to Create/Modify

- **Modify:** `crates/daemon/src/main.rs` — add `--run-bid-workflow <bid-job-id>` CLI subcommand parsing in the existing CLI argument handler. Pattern: find an existing `--<command>` subcommand in main.rs and mirror its shape.
- **Create:** `crates/daemon/tests/cli_bid_workflow.rs` — test that the CLI subcommand routes through the readiness evaluator.

## Implementation Details

The CLI subcommand:

```rust
// In main.rs argument parsing
if let Some(bid_job_id) = matches.value_of("run-bid-workflow") {
    // Load bid scope from existing workflow_jobs row (or accept --bid-scope-json path)
    let bid_scope = load_bid_scope_from_job(bid_job_id).await?;

    // Route through SAME readiness boundary as IPC
    let readiness = bid_workflow::evaluate_bid_readiness(&runtime, &bid_scope).await?;
    if !readiness.eligible {
        eprintln!("Bid readiness blocked: {:?}", readiness.blockers);
        std::process::exit(1);
    }

    // Build and enqueue
    let enqueue_req = enqueue_bid_workflow_request(...)?;
    let job_id = runtime.job_runner.enqueue_job(enqueue_req).await?;
    println!("Enqueued bid job: {}", job_id);
    return Ok(());
}
```

The test asserts the CLI cannot bypass readiness:

```rust
#[tokio::test]
async fn cli_run_bid_workflow_respects_readiness_gate() {
    let db = make_test_db_with_l5_blocker(&[ErrorCode::ClassificationAmbiguous]).await;
    // Simulate CLI invocation
    let result = run_cli(&["--run-bid-workflow", "test-bid-job-id"]).await;
    assert!(result.is_err()); // Or status != 0
    // No new workflow_jobs row created
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] CLI accepts `--run-bid-workflow <bid-job-id>`.
- [ ] CLI invocation calls `evaluate_bid_readiness` BEFORE any enqueue.
- [ ] Blocked readiness → CLI exits non-zero, no enqueue, prints blocker codes to stderr.
- [ ] Eligible readiness → enqueues exactly one `run_bid_workflow` job, prints `continuation_job_id` to stdout.
- [ ] CLI path does not duplicate readiness logic — it CALLS the same `evaluate_bid_readiness` as IPC.
- [ ] Test asserts CLI cannot bypass readiness gates.
- [ ] `cargo check --all-targets` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass.

## Dependencies

- **Blocked by:** `l6-p2-readiness-precheck-wiring`.
- **Blocks:** `l6-p2-daemon-runtime-review-gate`.
- **Phase:** 2.

# l6-p3-redaction-boundary-daemon

## SOURCE OF TRUTH WARNING

- **Spec**: §1.9.3 (web RLS — no sensitive fields in viewer projection), §2.5 (forward-compat — PDF extraction overlay) (PRIMARY)
- **TDD**: `...-tdd.md` — §7.13 `L6-T-redaction_boundary-001..006` (PRIMARY), §9.5 redaction contract (sentinel taxonomy)
- **Strategy**: Phase 3, "redaction sentinels" routing batch
- **Bootstrap**: §6 — manifest `test_redaction_boundary` notes (existing tests at redaction_boundary.rs)

## Coordination Protocol

`bin/br-claim` / `bin/br-complete`. Sync via `bin/br-sync`.

## Context

PII / company profile / BidScopePayload sentinels must NOT leak into error manifests, run manifests (agent narrative AND daemon evidence appendix), structured logs, tracing output, or Supabase projection payloads. This bead extends `crates/daemon/tests/redaction_boundary.rs` with the L6 sentinel taxonomy: company-profile sentinels (companyName, registrationNumber, vatNumber, address.* fields, primaryContact.* fields, certifications[].number, insurancePolicies[].policyNumber, insurancePolicies[].coverAmountPence, financialStatements.companiesHouseRef), BidScopePayload sentinels (raw process_id, lot_ids, candidate_ids, quote_ids, portal_opportunity_ref, local document paths, portal form values). Sentinels may only appear in authorized local daemon artifacts (which are already covered by artifact storage redaction policy). Audit-trail values (lot IDs, candidate IDs, quote IDs, company-profile version, screenshot refs, override IDs) may be cited as STABLE HASHES, not raw values, in the run manifest agent narrative.

## Spec Requirements (verbatim)

§9.5 Redaction Contract (from TDD): the sentinel classes must be injected by tests and absent from public/read-only surfaces.

**L6-FR-1.9.3 — Web visibility.** Read-only Supabase projection; viewer-role users cannot see sensitive `BidScopePayload` JSON or manifest content.

## TDD Tests Owned

- **L6-T-redaction_boundary-001** (T2): `error_manifests.error_context` and rendered `markdown_path` never contain raw company-profile sentinels.
- **L6-T-redaction_boundary-002** (T2): Error manifests may include stable hashes, field categories, and blocker codes for bid context — never raw BidScopePayload IDs, portal refs, local document paths, or portal form values.
- **L6-T-redaction_boundary-003** (T2): Hybrid run manifest `agent_narrative` omits company-profile sentinel fields while still citing lot IDs, candidate IDs, quote IDs, company-profile version, screenshot refs, and override IDs.
- **L6-T-redaction_boundary-004** (T2): Hybrid run manifest `daemon_evidence_appendix` records side-effect progression, readiness evidence, validator verdict, and artifact refs without raw contact, address, registration, VAT, certification, insurance, or financial statement values.
- **L6-T-redaction_boundary-005** (T2/T3): Supabase/web projections for `bid_workflow_states.bid_scope_json` expose only non-sensitive summary fields and hashes; viewer-role reads cannot recover raw BidScopePayload, company-profile, document path, or portal artifact values. (Cross-phase: Phase 6 `l6-p6-web-rls-grid` complements with role-scoped Supabase SELECT proof.)
