# l6-p3-state-machine-transitions

## SOURCE OF TRUTH WARNING

- **Spec**: `docs/strategy/layers/layer-6-request-pipeline-automation.md` — §1.3 state machine + 14 transition table rows (L6-FR-1.3.2..1.3.15) (PRIMARY)
- **TDD**: `...-tdd.md` — §7.1 `L6-T-bid_workflow_states-002..029` (14 transitions × happy/sad = 28 tests), §8.7 state transition proof matrix (PRIMARY)
- **Strategy**: Phase 3, "transition engine" routing batch
- **Bootstrap**: §6 — manifest references state machine layer-doc rows

## Coordination Protocol

`bin/br-claim` / `bin/br-complete`. Sync via `bin/br-sync`.

## Context

Implements the 14 lifecycle transitions in Rust with happy + sad paths. Each transition checks prerequisites BEFORE state change (no cached eligibility). Transitions write `bid_workflow_states` atomically — state, owner, row_version bump, stage_run_id, updated_at — wrapped in `write_push_owned_transaction`. Side-effect-aware transitions (e.g., `bid_in_progress → bid_failed` vs `bid_in_progress → portal_state_unknown` based on whether REMOTE_DRAFT+ was reached) are enforced here.

## Spec Requirements (verbatim)

L6-FR-1.3.2 — `not_started → ready_to_bid` (operator approves + not stale + L5 readiness passes).
L6-FR-1.3.3 — `ready_to_bid → bid_in_progress` (operator clicks Start Bid; prerequisites RE-verified).
L6-FR-1.3.4 — `ready_to_bid → not_started` (decision stale, L5 blocker activates, window expires, operator withdraws).
L6-FR-1.3.5 — `bid_in_progress → draft_saved` (skill saves draft on portal).
L6-FR-1.3.6 — `bid_in_progress → bid_submitted` (skill completes portal submission AND semantic validation clears; daemon compares stored decisionBasisHash against current — mismatch pauses to draft_saved).
L6-FR-1.3.7 — `bid_in_progress → bid_failed` (failure with no REMOTE_DRAFT+ side-effect; otherwise → portal_state_unknown).
L6-FR-1.3.8 — `bid_in_progress → portal_state_unknown` (crash/disconnect after REMOTE_DRAFT+, session timeout, operator cancel after REMOTE_DRAFT+).
L6-FR-1.3.9 — `draft_saved → bid_submitted` (operator confirms; reviewedBasisHash == current; validator approved or override).
L6-FR-1.3.10 — `draft_saved → bid_in_progress` (operator approves resume; prerequisites re-verified).
L6-FR-1.3.11 — `draft_saved → bid_failed` (operator abandons or final submission fails).
L6-FR-1.3.12 — `portal_state_unknown → bid_in_progress` (operator verifies + authorizes retry).
L6-FR-1.3.13 — `portal_state_unknown → bid_submitted` (operator confirms submission completed; manual confirmation ref).
L6-FR-1.3.14 — `portal_state_unknown → bid_failed` (operator determines unrecoverable).
L6-FR-1.3.15 — `bid_failed → ready_to_bid` (operator authorizes retry).

