## Coordination Protocol

`bin/br-claim` / `bin/br-complete`. Sync via `bin/br-sync`.

## Context

Two override flows in the desktop UI:
1. Quote-role override: when readiness shows `QUOTE_ROLE_FLOOR_ONLY` blocker, an "Override and acknowledge" button opens a structured form (reason text required + checkbox confirming awareness of floor-only evidence). Submission writes the override record to the database and adds an audit-trail entry that the run manifest will cite.
2. Validation gate override: when the run reaches `draft_saved` with validator rejection/outage, a "Override and submit final" button opens a structured form (reason text required + checkbox). Submission writes the override and proceeds to `bid_submitted`.

Both overrides require non-empty structured reason text + recorded_by + recorded_at; the override is recorded in `bid_workflow_states` metadata AND in the run manifest's daemon_evidence_appendix.

## Spec Requirements (verbatim)

**L6-FR-1.3.20 — Quote-role quality gate is enforced.** AC: `domestic_wholesale_floor`-only or `optimistic_floor`-only evidence blocks bid readiness unless the operator explicitly overrides with acknowledgment.

**L6-FR-1.3.23 — Validation policy is fail-closed for portal submission.** AC4: Operator may override the validation gate at final submission; the override is logged in bid state metadata and the run manifest.

